// Pull request: #6508 Add Windows rules for T1547.012 Print Processors persistence
// Pull request URL: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/pull/6508
// Pull request author: ali-vrd
// Change: new rule
// Title: Drop Binaries Into Print Processor Directory
// Sigma ID: 26138a6f-5c63-44ea-a341-c114530124bf
// Status: experimental | Level: high
// Author: ialivrd
// Date: 2026-10-22 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: persistence, privilege-escalation, T1547.012
// Description: Detects the creation of executable files inside the Windows print processor directory. Print
//   processors are DLLs that are loaded by the print spooler service (spoolsv.exe), which runs as
//   SYSTEM. Adversaries may drop malicious DLLs in this directory and register them for persistence
//   and/or privilege escalation as seen in the PipeMon campaign.
// False positives:
//   - Legitimate installation of printer software that ships its own print processor
// References:
//   - https://www.welivesecurity.com/2020/05/21/no-game-over-winnti-group/
//   - https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/win32/printdocs/addprintprocessor
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/4ff1a4fb9b90c019e441903afb0f48d3ec1a084e/rules/windows/file/file_event/file_event_win_susp_print_processor_folder_drop.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language, Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceFileEvents
| where (FolderPath contains "\\spool\\prtprocs\\" and (FolderPath endswith ".dll" or FolderPath endswith ".exe" or FolderPath endswith ".sys")) and (not(((InitiatingProcessFolderPath endswith "\\TrustedInstaller.exe" or InitiatingProcessFolderPath endswith "\\TiWorker.exe") or InitiatingProcessFolderPath endswith "\\spoolsv.exe")))
